 >
 > In **Dice Abyss**, a roll is an attack, a chest is a promise, and every new floor is another test of the equipment and talents you have assembled. The dungeon keeps going. So does your progression.
 
-## V5.20.0 · See the Odds Before You Pay.
-
-This complete archive is **cloud iteration 20**, based only on the supplied V5.19.0 archive. Extract it and follow [Run Locally](#run-locally) to play this version. The published website is maintained separately.
-
-**Make paid dice choices with the actual odds in view.** **命运赌桌** and **界外许愿** now show the probability of each outcome at your current luck. The wishing event explains that its two dice are independent; combat's matching-face guidance does not apply to that choice. These are distributions from the existing rules, with no prediction or advance roll of the next result.
-
-**Know the payment, refund and remaining budget.** See the full upfront cost, the balance immediately after payment, and the exact outcome-specific refund or balance. Odd prices use the same integer refund as the real transaction: paying 835 gold can return 417, for a net cost of 418. Gold from opening a resulting chest is accounted for later and is explicitly separate. An unaffordable choice states the exact shortfall without inventing a negative after-balance.
-
-**Compare chance with the guaranteed alternative.** The gambler's safe option keeps its original double-price payment. Each choice includes its net-spend and balance range. Expand **查看宝箱品质概率** to inspect all eight conditional rarity probabilities, including floor gates and the guaranteed alternative. Below floor 30 the gambler's named Rare/Epic rewards are exact; later rewards retain their original minimum-rarity rules.
-
-**Review the same information at confirmation.** The dialog repeats the selected choice's probability and budget information, and its action clearly says **支付并投骰** or **支付并选保底**. Cancelling preserves the complete save and restores focus. A change from another tab closes a stale review and refreshes the current odds. The wishing animation now correctly refers to two dice.
-
-The title, in-game footer, package and HTML release marker agree on **5.20.0**. This release retains **save schema 5**, original storage keys, V1–V4 migration, equipment IDs and unknown save fields. Existing inventory survival filters, comparisons, six-room routes, eight rarity gates, manual combat, 3D dice and offline fonts remain available. Combat, prices, rewards, RNG and storage transaction code are unchanged.
-
-The new tables and keyboard-operable disclosure follow the existing dark-metal style. No external runtime dependency, bitmap asset, font or audio file was added. Real browser checks, paired simulations and software-rendered timing limits are documented in [the current iteration report](docs/iteration/LATEST_REPORT.md). This release makes no general FPS, save-latency, optimal-budget or human win-rate improvement claim.
+## V5.21.0 · Read the Moment to Strike.
+
+This complete archive is **cloud iteration 21**, based only on the supplied V5.20.0 archive. Extract it and follow [Run Locally](#run-locally) to play this version. The published website is maintained separately.
+
+**See the two bandit deadlines separately.** The combat guide now shows the remaining opening-damage rolls and the remaining bonus-gold rolls, including the current roll. Against **拾金掠夺者**, the third roll can still win double gold after the +25% opening damage ends. Against **截路金匪**, the +15% damage and triple-gold windows both end after two rolls. Defeating either enemy still produces its normal chest after the bonus expires.
+
+**Know whether the first eligible critical is still available.** **启明星痕** and the matching equipment ability now explain the existing rule: the first critical while you hold the effect earns its luck once per enemy. An earlier critical without the effect does not spend that opportunity. The combat readout shows the available opportunity or **本场已触发**, independently of luck already earned for the next combat roll.
+
+**Read accurate instructions in an existing fight.** The exact inherited sentence that promised triple gold through the third roll now displays the correct two-roll deadline. This presentation correction preserves the raw saved narrative and custom notes. Talents, ability descriptions and equipment comparison use the same first-eligible critical wording.
+
+**Do less duplicate work when decoding a save.** A freshly parsed V5 save now reuses its validated inventory-ID set. The full expected-state comparison and public validation behavior remain intact; broader shortcuts were rejected after concrete compatibility counterexamples. See the measured scope and all retained tails in the iteration report.
+
+The title, in-game footer, package and HTML release marker agree on **5.21.0**. This release retains **save schema 5**, original storage keys, V1–V4 migration, equipment IDs and unknown save fields. Existing paid-event probability and budget previews, inventory survival filters, comparisons, six-room routes, eight rarity gates, manual combat, 3D dice and offline fonts remain available. Combat numbers, prices, rewards and RNG consumption remain unchanged.
+
+The new guidance and keyboard-operable disclosure follow the existing dark-metal style. No external runtime dependency, bitmap asset, font or audio file was added. Real browser checks, paired simulations, rejected optimization candidates and software-rendered timing limits are documented in [the current iteration report](docs/iteration/LATEST_REPORT.md). This release makes no general FPS, physical-disk durability, optimal-budget or human win-rate improvement claim.
 
